--- A list of whole numbers written down is a vector, which holds its
--- numbers as floats: a computed whole number up to 2^53 is held exactly,
--- and one past it stops where the list is made, in both modes, naming
--- `push`. It had been rounded silently — `[a, 3]` with `a = 2 ^ 60 + 1`
--- held 2^60, and `xs[0] eq a` was false (Rosetta Code, Abundant odd
--- numbers; Vijay, 2026-10-29). A list grown with push keeps every digit.
a = 2 ^ 53
xs = [a, 3]
log[xs[0]]
b = 2 ^ 60 + 1
kept = push[push[[], b], 3]
log[kept[0] eq b]
ys = [b, 3]
log[ys[0]]
